Our goal is to build a system that:

    Starts with a fully functional, pre-configured website-builder team.

    Has a clear, simple feedback loop for end-of-project review.

    Includes a powerful, specialized "Prompt Agent" to handle the evolution of agents when flagged for improvement.

    Follows your principle of creating new agent instances/definitions for any changes.

Phase 1: The Foundation (Static Prompts & High-Level Feedback)

In this phase, we'll get the core website-builder working perfectly using pre-defined prompts and add the simple, end-of-workflow human review step.

Step 1.1: Create a Comprehensive Migration for Agent Definitions

You are correct, we should fully populate the initial configurations so we have a solid V1 to evolve from.

    Action: Create a new migration file (e.g., 009_seed_website_builder_definitions.sql).

    Content: This script will contain an INSERT statement for every agent type used by the website builder (domain-analyst, site-architect, html-developer, visual-designer, site-publisher).

    Pseudo-code (SQL Example for html-developer):
