Phase 2: The Evolution Loop & Dynamic Prompt Creation

This phase implements the specialized Prompt Agent, triggered by the "Flag for Improvement" action.

Step 2.1: Define the "Prompt Improvement Agent"

    Action: Add a new entry to your agent_definitions migration for this specialized agent.

    Pseudo-code (SQL):
    SQL

    INSERT INTO agent_definitions (type, display_name, ..., default_config) VALUES
    ('prompt-improvement-agent', 'Prompt Improvement Agent', ..., '{
        "ai_service": { "provider": "anthropic", "model": "claude-3-opus-20240229" },
        "prompt_template": "You are a Prompt Engineering expert. The provided prompt for an agent of type {{.input.agent_type}} has performed poorly... Analyze the prompt and the failure context, then generate an improved prompt. Failure Context: {{.input.failure_context}}. Old Prompt: {{.input.old_prompt}}",
        "workflow": {
            "start_step": "generate_new_prompt",
            "steps": {
                "generate_new_prompt": { "action": "execute_llm_prompt", "next_step": "human_approval" },
                "human_approval": { "action": "pause_for_human_input", "config": {...}, "next_step": "save_new_version" },
                "save_new_version": { "action": "save_new_agent_definition", "next_step": "complete" },
                "complete": { "action": "complete_workflow" }
            }
        }
    }'::jsonb);

Step 2.2: Implement the save_new_agent_definition Action

This is the key to making your system "learn." It's a powerful admin-level action that creates a new, versioned agent definition.

    Action: Create a new local action in Go.

    Pseudo-code (Go):
    Go

    // in a new file, e.g., platform/orchestration/actions/admin_actions.go
    func SaveNewAgentDefinitionAction(ctx context.Context, params ActionParams) (interface{}, error) {
        // 1. Get the approved prompt from `params.CollectedData["human_feedback"]`.
        // 2. Get the original agent type (e.g., "html-developer") from the initial request data.
        // 3. Determine the next version number (e.g., if "html-developer" exists, this becomes "html-developer-v2").
        // 4. Read the full definition of the original agent from the `agent_definitions` table.
        // 5. Create a new definition object, copying all fields but updating:
        //    - The `type` name to the new versioned name.
        //    - The `prompt_template` to the new, human-approved prompt.
        // 6. INSERT this new object as a new row into the `agent_definitions` table.
        // 7. Return the new agent type name (e.g., "html-developer-v2").
    }

